<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to September 25 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.35 (0.35)	 one year     0.42 (0.42)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.35 (0.35)	 two years    0.63 (0.66)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.36 (0.37)	 three years  1.19 (1.21)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.37 (0.38)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.58 (0.60)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.31 (0.32)	 three years  1.14 (1.17)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.32 (0.33)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.52 (0.55)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.27 (0.27)	 three years  1.09 (1.12)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Sept 24- Sept 27:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.56 (0.52)   120-150 days  UNQ  (0.50)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.53 (0.54)   150-180 days  0.55 (0.57)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.53 (0.53)   180-360 days  0.56 (0.56)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.57 (0.53)   over 360 days 1.24 (UNQ )</p>
